                        <chunk name="InputParam" index="1">
                          <items count="9">
                            <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Slice of the year to output: Year (default), a season, or a single month. Every hourly output is cut to that period's hours, Hour of Year included, so the HOY list can drive UTCI, Sun Hours or any other HOY input for the same hours. Seasons are named by their months (Winter = Dec-Feb), so a southern-hemisphere EPW reads unambiguously. Header values (Latitude, Elevation, ...) are not hourly and are never cut.</item>
                            <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">d319df12-ac50-4b9d-885e-b5833f3416ba</item>
