                    <chunk name="param_input" index="6">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How the preview and the Colored Mesh output colour the ground. 'Land use' paints each zone by what it is (water, grass &amp; parks, forest, paved, residential, ...); 'Roughness' paints it by z0 on a FIXED logarithmic scale anchored on the eight Davenport classes (0.0002 m pale yellow to 2 m dark brown), so a z0 has the same colour in every document and component. Terrain no zone covers is grey in both. Display only: the zones, their z0 and the written case are identical either way.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">92e7276b-3615-4844-a1b3-a944b15f7532</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
