                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">PIMPLE only: averaging time constant in SECONDS. A transient run's U is an instantaneous, gusty snapshot, so the case also writes UMean/pMean (plus UPrime2Mean, the resolved variance) - read THOSE downstream, not U. The window damps the start-up transient exponentially, weighting a contribution by about exp(-age/window); it does NOT hard-cut it, because OpenFOAM 12's fieldAverage has no timeStart. So keep the run long relative to the window. 0 or blank uses half the Duration. Optional.</item>
